{"step_index":1195,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T02:28:29Z","input_tokens":4740,"cache_read_tokens":206369,"output_tokens":2309,"thinking":"Initial inspection of the \"Unrelaxed AIMD\" calculation output reveals a critical point. Every detail warrants careful consideration, specifically the specifics of this simulation. This contrasts with earlier assumptions.\n\n\nThe \"Unrelaxed AIMD\" calculation exhibits consistent SCF convergence across all steps, contrary to initial expectations. Temperature and energy profiles indicate significant surface relaxation occurring within the initial steps as atoms seek their optimal positions. This relaxation process releases potential energy, converting it into kinetic energy, and represents dynamic reconstruction.\n\n\nThe unrelaxed AIMD simulation displays significant temperature fluctuations linked to surface reconstruction. Energy release during this relaxation nearly cancels the kinetic energy drop. The total energy remains exceptionally stable throughout the simulation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_env_rtx5080/bin/python3 -c \\\"\\nimport os, numpy as np\\n\\nunrel_dir = 'aimd_2H-SiC_10-10_8periods_vac3.0A_unrelaxed_300K_100steps_rtx5080'\\nwith open(os.path.join(unrel_dir, 'dump.lammpstrj')) as f:\\n    lines = f.readlines()\\n\\nframes = []\\ni = 0\\nwhile i < len(lines):\\n    if 'ITEM: TIMESTEP' in lines[i]:\\n        step = int(lines[i+1].strip())\\n        natoms = int(lines[i+3].strip())\\n        data = []\\n        for l in lines[i+9:i+9+natoms]:\\n            parts = l.split()\\n            data.append([int(parts[0]), int(parts[1]), float(parts[2]), float(parts[3]), float(parts[4])])\\n        data.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\\n        frames.append((step, np.array(data)))\\n        i += 9 + natoms\\n    else:\\n        i += 1\\n\\ninit_pos = frames[0][1][:, 2:5]\\ntypes = frames[0][1][:, 1].astype(int) # 1: C, 2: Si\\natom_ids = frames[0][1][:, 0].astype(int)\\nz0 = init_pos[:, 2]\\n\\n# In unrelaxed slab: z_min = 3.0000 (Layer 1), z_max = 22.5354 (Layer 16)\\nbot_mask = z0 < 3.5\\ntop_mask = z0 > 22.0\\n\\nall_dz = np.array([arr[:, 4] - z0 for _, arr in frames]) # (101, 288)\\nall_dist = np.array([np.linalg.norm(arr[:, 2:5] - init_pos, axis=1) for _, arr in frames])\\n\\n# Top surface (Layer 16): outward is +dz, inward is -dz\\ntop_dz = all_dz[:, top_mask]\\ntop_types = types[top_mask]\\n# Bottom surface (Layer 1): outward is -dz, inward is +dz\\nbot_dz = all_dz[:, bot_mask]\\nbot_types = types[bot_mask]\\n\\nprint('=== UNRELAXED AIMD: INWARD vs OUTWARD SURFACE DISPLACEMENT ===')\\nprint(f'Top surface (Layer 16):')\\nprint(f'  Max OUTWARD (+dz, into vacuum): {top_dz.max():+.4f} A (Si max: {top_dz[:, top_types==2].max():+.4f} A, C max: {top_dz[:, top_types==1].max():+.4f} A)')\\nprint(f'  Max INWARD  (-dz, into slab)  : {top_dz.min():+.4f} A (Si min: {top_dz[:, top_types==2].min():+.4f} A, C min: {top_dz[:, top_types==1].min():+.4f} A)')\\nprint(f'Bottom surface (Layer 1):')\\nprint(f'  Max OUTWARD (-dz, into vacuum): {(-bot_dz).max():+.4f} A (Si max: {(-bot_dz[:, bot_types==2]).max():+.4f} A,\n<truncated 838 bytes>","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Analyze inward vs outward surface displacements in unrelaxed AIMD\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
